  "lesson": {
    "slug": "photon-interactions",
    "title": "Photon Interactions with Matter",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "What Happens When a Photon Hits Tissue",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "When an X-ray or gamma ray photon passes through a medium, it interacts with the matter and transfers energy to it. That first energy transfer ejects electrons from atoms in the medium, which then produce further ionization and excitation along their own path."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Four things can happen to a photon in the beam: "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "absorption",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " (energy taken up by tissue), "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "scattering",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " (change in direction), "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "transmission",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " (passes through unaffected), or a combination. "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Attenuation",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " is the overall removal of photons from the beam by either absorption or scattering combined."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Attenuation Coefficients and HVL",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "linear attenuation coefficient (\u03bc)",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " expresses the probability of a photon being removed by a given material per unit thickness, for a monoenergetic beam. It's related to the "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Half-Value Layer (HVL)",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " \u2014 the thickness of material needed to cut beam intensity in half \u2014 by:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "\u03bc = 0.693 / HVL",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "\u03bc depends on the density of the material, which makes it a less fundamental property than it first appears \u2014 compressing a layer of material to half its thickness (doubling its density) won't actually change its attenuation. The "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "mass attenuation coefficient",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " (\u03bc/\u03c1, linear coefficient divided by density) corrects for this."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Five Ways a Photon Can Interact",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Which interaction happens depends heavily on the photon's energy. The simulator on the next page lets you explore all five interactively:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
